<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">19072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Israeli strikes killed fourteen people in Gaza this week, the highest weekly toll since the ceasefire took hold.</s> <s>A truce that exists on paper has not stopped the dying, as Israel pushes what it calls its Yellow Line onto Gaza's main north-south road.</s> <s>Israel hasn't said when the advance halts, leaving the only route linking the enclave's north and south in question.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's Civilian Joint Task Force has named a retired general to command it, formalising a militia that grew up beside the army's war against Boko Haram.</s> <s>Born fifteen years ago as a state-backed auxiliary in the north-east, the force fights, detains, and has faced accusations of abuse in the same theatre as regular troops.</s> <s>Its chairman promises a formal command blueprint soon, but the deeper question is who holds an armed body outside the chain of command to account.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Amman, Iranian missiles killed two American soldiers at the Muwaffaq Salti base in Jordan, the Pentagon said, the first combat deaths of this war.</s> <s>The base hosts the largest US tactical-air contingent in the Middle East, and a seventh straight night of American strikes hit an Iranian desalination plant, cutting water to ten thousand people.</s> <s>Once both sides target water and power, the war stops degrading armies and begins degrading the civilian systems ordinary people depend on.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Hungary's president, Tamas Sulyok, signed the very amendment that ends his own term, saying he had no legal path to resist it.</s> <s>The new government of Peter Magyar is using constitutional change to remove the head of state, the same tool Viktor Orban wielded for fifteen years.</s> <s>Hungary's constitution has become an instrument of whoever commands a two-thirds majority, and lawmakers must now elect a successor within thirty days.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Near Tyre in southern Lebanon, a blast killed one Lebanese soldier and wounded two others as their vehicle entered a security zone.</s> <s>Israel's military says the device likely belonged to Hezbollah, in ground still contested months after a supposed ceasefire.</s> <s>The Lebanese army has opened an investigation, but the incident shows how unresolved the frontier remains.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Fifty-three thousand tonnes of steel just moved through Gwadar Port on Pakistan's Makran coast, transshipped from a Bangladesh-flagged vessel toward the Emirates.</s> <s>Transshipment means cargo pauses at one port before continuing to another, and as the Strait of Hormuz becomes a war zone, a working deep-sea port is a hedge against chokepoint risk.</s> <s>That Gwadar kept operating uninterrupted through the tensions next door is itself the news, and a vindication of China's long bet on the corridor.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Baghdad signed forty-eight deals with American firms, and Chevron will rebuild the Kirkuk-to-Baniyas pipeline through Syria.</s> <s>The corridor would give Iraq two million barrels a day flowing to the Mediterranean, bypassing the Strait of Hormuz entirely.</s> <s>The US ambassador says it will make Hormuz an afterthought, though a pipeline through Syria carries risks of its own.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesia has named Morocco its gateway to North Africa, betting on the kingdom's free-trade deals with the European Union and the continent.</s> <s>Morocco's Tangier port and its web of agreements offer Jakarta a launchpad into African markets, a South-South route around the old colonial trade maps.</s> <s>Neither government has announced tariffs, volumes, or a start date, so the ambition still outruns the detail.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington will impose a twenty-five percent tariff on Brazil on <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22072026</say-as>, striking at Pix, the free instant-payment system used by ninety percent of Brazilian adults.</s> <s>Pix broke the grip of card networks and banks, and dollar-pegged stablecoins already ride the same digital rails.</s> <s>Taxing a country's payment infrastructure is a new kind of leverage, and it may only deepen Brazil's turn toward alternatives to the dollar.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In Venezuela, government-built housing towers fell like sandcastles, and the National Assembly now puts the earthquake toll at five thousand and sixty-nine, with fifty thousand still missing.</s> <s>Engineers blame the absence of any anti-seismic standards in state-built homes, a failure of construction as much as of geology.</s> <s>Venezuela has drawn three hundred and forty-six million dollars from its reserves, while some twenty thousand people remain without shelter.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Beneath Bhutan, researchers used three hundred and thirteen local earthquakes to map hidden faults deep in the crust.</s> <s>Seismic waves split as they cross fractured rock, letting scientists read stress and deformation as far as thirty-five kilometres underground, where the Indian and Asian plates grind together.</s> <s>The findings, still awaiting peer review, offer a rare window into earthquake hazard across an under-instrumented mountain kingdom.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Across England and Wales, researchers estimate that heat killed more than two thousand seven hundred people this May and June.</s> <s>Heat rarely appears on a death certificate, so scientists used rapid-attribution modelling to count the deaths the official record misses.</s> <s>Not one of those two thousand seven hundred will be formally listed as a victim of the heat that took them.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>France has ordered internet providers to block Polymarket, becoming the thirtieth-plus country to firewall the crypto prediction market.</s> <s>A transaction ban failed when two hundred and five thousand French users visited in June, many slipping past it with a virtual private network, so the regulator is now blocking the platform at the network's edge.</s> <s>It's internet governance by chokepoint, colliding with a market built to be censorship-resistant, and violators face fines up to one hundred thousand euros.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>From Sriharikota, India's Skyroot Aerospace placed six payloads in orbit on its rocket's very first attempt.</s> <s>The twenty-two-metre vehicle makes India the third nation with a private company capable of reaching orbit, after the United States and China.</s> <s>Skyroot plans more test flights before it begins routine commercial missions in the small-satellite market, God willing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Over Kuwait's Al-Shuaiba, Google downgraded satellite resolution across a power plant, a desalination facility, refineries, and the port, Iranian state media reported.</s> <s>The blurring followed Iran's retaliatory strikes on US-linked sites, and a private firm quietly editing the resolution of war evidence is a power few noticed it held.</s> <s>Planet Labs has separately imposed a ninety-six-hour delay on its imagery, leaving the public record of the strikes in corporate hands.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At Kaiser Permanente in California, advice nurses say call-length timers and AI tone-scoring now factor into their performance reviews.</s> <s>One suicidal caller's plea for help became a manager's complaint about time, seven nurses told reporters, as software judged the care by the clock.</s> <s>The California Nurses Association is fighting to write limits on the technology into Kaiser's next contract.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>